From: Tomato64 <noreply@tomato64>
Subject: [PATCH] do not re-add an existing IA_NA address on renewal

update_address() calls na_ifaddrconf(IFADDRCONF_ADD) whenever the lease
has a non-zero valid lifetime, including for an address that is merely
being renewed and is therefore already configured on the interface.

On Linux ifaddrconf() performs the add with ioctl(SIOCSIFADDR), which
fails with EEXIST in that case. The failure is not logged - only the
remove path reports errors - but update_address() still returns early on
it, so the code below never runs and the address timer keeps the deadline
computed at first acquisition. A renewed address then expires on the
original schedule and addr_timo() removes it, even though the server
renewed it. The ioctl also carries no lifetimes on Linux, so the re-add
could not refresh them even if it succeeded.

Configure the address only when it is first created, which is what the
prefix path in prefixconf.c already does with its spcreate check, and let
a renewal fall through to the timer update.

diff --git a/addrconf.c b/addrconf.c
index 13ad88b..5978fea 100644
--- a/addrconf.c
+++ b/addrconf.c
@@ -170,7 +170,7 @@ update_address(struct ia *ia, struct dhcp6_statefuladdr *addr,
 	    ", vltime=%" PRIu32, sacreate ? "create" : "update",
 	    in6addr2str(&addr->addr, 0), addr->pltime, addr->vltime);
 
-	if (sa->addr.vltime != 0) {
+	if (sacreate && sa->addr.vltime != 0) {
 		if (na_ifaddrconf(IFADDRCONF_ADD, sa) < 0) {
 			/* XXX no reporting here either */
 			return (-1);
